# AutoKuma — copy to services/autokuma/.env on the box. See docs/MONITORING.md.

# ─── Kuma admin credentials ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AutoKuma drives Kuma's internal Socket.IO API, which means a real login.
# There is no scoped/service account in Kuma, so this IS the admin credential —
# store it in Vaultwarden as a Tier-2 secret, same as the one you typed into
# the setup wizard.
#
# NOTE: nothing can bootstrap the admin account — Kuma's first-run wizard is
# always manual. Claim it in the same session you deploy Kuma; an unclaimed
# wizard on a public vhost is open to whoever finds it first
# (docs/SECURITY_PASS.md, SEC-2).
AUTOKUMA__KUMA__USERNAME=admin
AUTOKUMA__KUMA__PASSWORD=

# ─── Push tokens ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These make the dead-man's-switch URLs DETERMINISTIC. Because AutoKuma can pin
# a push token, the URL is known before the monitor exists — so the token flows
# straight into services/backup/.env and services/smart/.env instead of the old
# dance of creating a monitor in the UI, copying its generated token, and
# pasting it back. setup.sh generates these and wires them through.
#
# Format is enforced by AutoKuma: EXACTLY 32 characters, letters and digits
# only. `openssl rand -hex 16` produces a valid one. A malformed token doesn't
# fail loudly — the monitor is skipped and AutoKuma logs a WARN every sync
# cycle, so the monitor silently never appears. If a push monitor is missing,
# check `docker logs autokuma` first.
#
# Treat these as secrets: anyone holding one can post a fake "all is well"
# heartbeat and keep a monitor looking green while the real job is failing.
# That's why the templates are rendered on the box and never committed.
#
# Two of these are for hosts that are NOT on the coralstack docker network —
# the Proxmox hypervisor and the Mac mini. Their heartbeats can't use
# http://uptime-kuma:3001, so setup.sh can't write the URL into a file for
# them; it prints the public https://status.<domain>/api/push/<token> form at
# the end of its run instead, to be pasted into the host by hand.
BACKUP_PUSH_TOKEN=
SMART_APPS_PUSH_TOKEN=
SMART_HOST_PUSH_TOKEN=
DRIFT_PUSH_TOKEN=
OLLAMA_MINI_PUSH_TOKEN=
